1. Definitions

"Software" means the software in the repository or package that contains this
License file, including its source code, object code, documentation, runtime
card templates, and examples, in every version, together with any portion of
it. Third-party code included in it stays under its own license.

"Licensor" means Jason Blasiak.

"You" means the person or entity that obtains the Software and accepts this
License. For Section 2, "You" means a single natural person. For Section 2A,
"You" means a Small Business.

"Immediate Family Member" means Your spouse or domestic partner, parent,
child, or sibling.

"Personal Use" means use of the Software by You, and by no more than three (3)
of Your Immediate Family Members, solely:
  (a) on computers and devices that You or that Immediate Family Member
      personally own and that are not owned, leased, managed, or provided by
      any Organization; and
  (b) for private, personal, non-commercial purposes that are unrelated to
      any job, employment, trade, profession, business, or Organization.

"Organization" means any corporation, company, partnership, sole
proprietorship, limited liability company, business, nonprofit, association,
school, university, hospital, laboratory, government body or agency, or any
other institution or legal entity of any kind, together with its owners,
officers, directors, employees, contractors, and agents when acting for it.

"Affiliate" means any entity that controls, is controlled by, or is under
common control with another entity.

"Small Business" means a for-profit Organization that, together with all of
its Affiliates:
  (a) had total gross revenue of less than US$1,000,000 (or the equivalent in
      another currency) in its most recently completed financial year (or,
      if it has not completed one, expects less than that in its first
      financial year); and
  (b) is not valued at US$1,000,000 or more, measured by the post-money
      valuation of its most recent priced equity financing or, if it has had
      none in the last 24 months, by a good-faith valuation made in the last
      24 months; and
  (c) is not a government body, and is not controlled by or an Affiliate of
      an Organization that is not itself a Small Business.

"Registration" means a written notice to the Licensor, sent to the
registration address in Section 10, stating: the Organization's legal name and
country; a contact person and address; confirmation that it meets the
definition of Small Business and the revenue band for its last financial year
(under US$1,000,000); which Software it uses; the products or services it
uses the Software in; and the date it first used the Software.

"Commercial License" means a separate written license agreement signed by the
Licensor, which may require license fees and royalties.

2. Personal Use (free)

Subject to Your compliance with this License, the Licensor grants You a
personal, non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, revocable,
royalty-free license, for Personal Use only, to:
  (a) download, view, and read the Software;
  (b) install and run the Software on Your personal devices to try it out and
      to create and operate Your own personal runtime environments; and
  (c) create Your own configurations using the Software's documented
      interfaces, without altering the Software itself.
Personal Use is limited to You and no more than three (3) Immediate Family
Members in total.

2A. Small Business Grant (free, with Registration)

For as long as You are a Small Business, have Registered, and comply with this
Section 2A, the Licensor grants You a non-exclusive, non-transferable,
non-sublicensable, royalty-free license to:
  (a) use the Software inside Your Organization, on Your own or Your
      Organization's devices and infrastructure;
  (b) modify the Software for Your own use and for use in Your products and
      services;
  (c) incorporate the Software, unmodified or modified, as a component of a
      larger product or service of Yours that adds substantial functionality
      of its own, and provide that product or service to Your customers,
      whether installed or hosted; Your customers receive no right to the
      Software apart from using it as part of Your product or service.

Conditions of Section 2A:
  (i)   Registration. You must Register within thirty (30) days after You
        first use the Software, and renew Your Registration within thirty
        (30) days after the end of each of Your financial years by confirming
        in writing that You still meet the definition of Small Business and
        stating Your revenue band.
  (ii)  Records and verification. You must keep records that show You meet the
        definition of Small Business. Once in any twelve months the Licensor
        may ask You in writing for a short written statement of those facts,
        and You must answer within thirty (30) days. There is no on-site
        audit.
  (iii) The registry. The Licensor keeps a register of Registrations for
        transparency and auditing. The Licensor may disclose it to auditors,
        regulators, and where the law requires, and may publish totals and
        statistics. The Licensor will not publish Your name without Your
        consent.
  (iv)  Outgrowing the limit. If You stop being a Small Business, Your rights
        under this Section 2A continue for ninety (90) days after the end of
        the financial year in which You stopped, during which You must either
        obtain a Commercial License or stop using the Software and destroy
        all copies. Crossing the limit part-way through a financial year does
        not by itself end Your rights until that year ends.
  (v)   Notices. You must keep every copyright, patent, and license notice in
        the Software and include a copy of this License with any copy of the
        Software You provide as part of Section 2A(c).
  (vi)  No stand-alone redistribution. You may not make the Software, or a
        modification of it, available to others as an SDK, library, or
        service in its own right, or in a product whose main value is the
        Software itself.

3. What Requires a Commercial License

Unless Section 2 or Section 2A applies, You may NOT do any of the following
without a Commercial License:
  (a) use the Software in or for any Organization, at any level and in any
      role, including use by an owner, officer, director, employee,
      contractor, or agent for any work or business purpose, or on any
      device, network, or account owned, leased, managed, or provided by an
      Organization;
  (b) alter, modify, adapt, translate, or create derivative works of the
      Software;
  (c) distribute, publish, share, sublicense, rent, lease, lend, host, or
      otherwise make the Software, or any portion or modification of it,
      available to any person other than as Section 2 or Section 2A
      expressly allows, in source or compiled form, whether or not for a fee;
  (d) sell the Software, or any product, service, device, or work that
      incorporates, embeds, is built on, or is derived from the Software or
      any portion of it;
  (e) use the Software to generate revenue or other commercial advantage,
      directly or indirectly, including by offering it as a hosted or managed
      service or by using it to provide services to others; or
  (f) remove, alter, or obscure any copyright, patent, or license notice in
      the Software.
Each of these needs its own Commercial License and is subject to the fees and
royalties stated in it.

